    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passed, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all owner duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey`.\n\n**The key** (`IdentityKeyResolver.deriveIdentityKey`):\n```\n<normalizedTelephone> | <email or empty> | <householdId or empty>\n```\nIt canonicalizes the telephone (E.164) and email (lower-cased) the same way for both the new and existing owners, and treats a missing email or household as empty.\n\n**Consolidated check** (`OwnerRestControllerV1`):\n- Removed the three separate checks \u2014 `requireUniqueTelephone`, `requireUniqueEmail`, and `requireUniqueHousehold` \u2014 from `normalizeAndValidate`.\n- Added `requireUniqueIdentity(owner)`, which rejects with **409** only when the new owner's *whole* `identityKey` equals an existing owner's.\n- Reordered so `assignHouseholdId` runs *before* the check (the key needs the assigned `householdId`), and annotated `addOwner` with `@Transactional` so a rejected create rolls back any household backfill.\n\n**Behaviour change, as specified:** because the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have different keys and are both allowed; only an exact full-key match is a duplicate. The given acceptance test \u2014 two otherwise-unique owners sharing a telephone (both with empty email and null household) \u2192 identical key \u2192 409 \u2014 passes.\n\n**Returning `identityKey`:**\n- Added a read-only `identityKey` to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`.\n- The controller stamps it onto every owner response (`addOwner`, `getOwner`, `listOwners`) via a `toOwnerDto` helper, since it isn't a stored field the MapStruct mapper can produce (`identityKey` is marked `ignore` in the mapper).\n\n**Cleanup:** deleted the now-unused `DuplicateTelephoneException` and `DuplicateEmailException` classes and their advice handlers; repurposed `DuplicateOwnerException` (and its handler) as the single identity-collision exception.\n\nOne note: the V2 paged endpoint (`OwnerRestControllerV2`) maps owners directly through the mapper, so its page items won't carry `identityKey` \u2014 I kept that path untouched since it's a read endpoint outside the create/duplicate flow and no test exercises it. Let me know if you'd like `identityKey` populated there too.",
